Your provided MATLAB code is a good approach to finding the unique words in Text1 that do not appear in Text2. It can handle a large amount of text by reading the texts from files instead of storing them as strings in memory. Here's a slight modification to make it more efficient:

```matlab
function unique_words = find_unique_words(text1_file, text2_file)
    text1 = fileread(text1_file);
    text2 = fileread(text2_file);

    % Convert text to lowercase and split into words
    words1 = lower(strsplit(text1));
    words2 = lower(strsplit(text2));

    % Find unique words in text1 that do not appear in text2
    unique_words = setdiff(words1, words2);
end
```

This function takes two file names as input and returns a vector containing the unique words in Text1 that do not appear in Text2. You can call this function with your specific file names like this:

