To pass credentials in JavaScript code for `react-native-fbsdk-next`, you can follow these steps:

1. First, make sure you have installed the required dependencies:

```bash
npm install react-native-fbsdk-next
```

2. Create a new file named `Credentials.js` and add the following code:

```javascript
import { FacebookAuthProvider } from 'react-native-fbsdk-next';

const credentials = new FacebookAuthProvider();
credentials.setCredentials({
  accessToken: 'YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN',
  expiresIn: 'YOUR_EXPIRES_IN',
});

export default credentials;
```

Replace `YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN` and `YOUR_EXPIRES_IN` with your actual Facebook access token and expiration time.

3. Now, you can import the `Credentials` object in your other components and use it to authenticate users:

```javascript
import React, { useState } from 'react';
import { View, Text, Button } from 'react-native';
import Credentials from './Credentials';

const MyComponent = () => {
  const [isAuthenticated, setIsAuthenticated] = useState(false);

  const handleLogin = async () => {
    try {
      await Credentials.loginWithReadPermissionsAsync();
      setIsAuthenticated(true);
    } catch (error) {
      console.error('Login failed:', error);
    }
  };

  return (
    <View>
      <Text>{isAuthenticated ? 'Logged in' : 'Not logged in'}</Text>
      <Button title="Login" onPress={handleLogin} />
    </View>
  );
};

export default MyComponent;
```

That's it! With this setup, you can pass credentials in JavaScript code for `react-native-fbsdk-next`. Make sure to replace the `accessToken` and `expiresIn` values with your actual Facebook access token and expiration time.

