4. Industrial processes - emissions from cement production, chemical manufacturing, etc.
5. Transportation - emissions from cars, trucks, planes, and ships
6. Energy consumption - emissions from power plants, heating, and cooling systems
7. Waste management - emissions from landfills and incinerators
8. Forest fires - release CO2 stored in trees and vegetation
9. Permafrost melting - releases methane and CO2 as the permafrost thaws
10. Ocean acidification - as CO2 dissolves in the ocean, it makes the water more acidic, affecting marine life and ecosystems.

